{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_0117DuK4HdxRAJv768Wi1AsB","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# Checklist for `true-bdd us apply <story-id>`.\n2\t# Walk every AC in the refined story and merge each one into the registry\n3\t# (docs/scenarios.yaml).\n4\t#\n5\t# Engine-test prompt set: intentionally minimal (2 prompts) to exercise the\n6\t# many-scenarios × many-prompts walk and the per-cell fix loop. Will be\n7\t# expanded with richer merge-correctness checks once the engine is proven.\n8\t\n9\tversion: \"1.0\"\n10\tlast_updated: \"2026-04-25\"\n11\t# Per-checklist engine knob, read by `us apply --fix` to bound the outer\n12\t# re-walk loop: any fix applied during walk N re-walks from AC 1 prompt 1;\n13\t# N reaching max_apply_attempts without a clean walk aborts, registry untouched.\n14\tconfig:\n15\t    max_apply_attempts: 5\n16\tsections:\n17\t    - id: merge\n18\t      name: \"Scenario Merge\"\n19\t      description: \"Each AC from the story must be present, and only once, in the registry.\"\n20\t      validation_prompts:\n21\t        - Q: |\n22\t            Does this acceptance criterion already appear as a scenario in the\n23\t            registry?\n24\t\n25\t            The registry is the requirements YAML referenced by the subject\n26\t            (the scratch copy for this run). An AC \"appears\" when there is an\n27\t            entry under `scenarios:` whose `user_stories[]` list contains the\n28\t            subject's story path AND the subject's lineage scenario id.\n29\t\n30\t            Pass when at least one such entry exists.\n31\t            Fail otherwise.\n32\t\n33\t            Context: emit one line.\n34\t              - \"AC <ac id> (lineage <lineage id>): present in <matched scenario id>\"\n35\t              - \"AC <ac id> (lineage <lineage id>): not present\"\n36\t          rationale: \"Every refined-story AC must be reflected as a tracked scenario in the registry.\"\n37\t          F: |\n38\t            Add this AC as a new scenario in the registry.\n39\t\n40\t            Use the Edit tool against the registry file referenced by the\n41\t            subject. Steps:\n42\t              1. Pick the next free id following existing numbering — `INT-NNN`\n43\t                 for integration-layer ACs, `E2E-NNN` for e2e-layer ACs. If\n44\t                 unsure, prefer `E2E-NNN`. Do not reuse an existing id.\n45\t              2. Insert a new entry under `scenarios:` with:\n46\t                    description: <short summary derived from the AC description>\n47\t                    service: \"\"\n48\t                    path: <see below>\n49\t                    last_updated: \"<today, YYYY-MM-DD>\"\n50\t                    user_stories:\n51\t                      - story: <story file path from subject>\n52\t                        scenario_id: <lineage id from subject>\n53\t                        merge_date: \"<today, YYYY-MM-DD>\"\n54\t                    merged_steps:\n55\t                      given: <verbatim from the AC's steps.given>\n56\t                      when:  <verbatim from the AC's steps.when>\n57\t                      then:  <verbatim from the AC's steps.then>\n58\t              3. `path:` names the generated test file this scenario's Go\n59\t                 test is written into. REUSE an existing `path:` from a\n60\t                 scenario of the same command or feature family — several\n61\t                 scenarios share one file on purpose, so related\n62\t                 behaviours are read together. Invent a new one only when\n63\t                 no existing file fits, and then make it\n64\t                 `<suite path>/<family>_test.go`, where <suite path> is\n65\t                 the tests/<service>/ tree of the scenario\n66\t                 whose `service:` matches this scenario's.\n67\t              4. Preserve existing file ordering and indentation. Do not\n68\t                 touch any other entry.\n69\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":