 the registry.\n\n            Use the Edit tool against the registry file referenced by the\n            subject. Steps:\n              1. Pick the next free id following existing numbering — `INT-NNN`\n                 for integration-layer ACs, `E2E-NNN` for e2e-layer ACs. If\n                 unsure, prefer `E2E-NNN`. Do not reuse an existing id.\n              2. Insert a new entry under `scenarios:` with:\n                    description: <short summary derived from the AC description>\n                    service: \"\"\n                    path: <see below>\n                    last_updated: \"<today, YYYY-MM-DD>\"\n                    user_stories:\n                      - story: <story file path from subject>\n                        scenario_id: <lineage id from subject>\n                        merge_date: \"<today, YYYY-MM-DD>\"\n                    merged_steps:\n                      given: <verbatim from the AC's steps.given>\n                      when:  <verbatim from the AC's steps.when>\n                      then:  <verbatim from the AC's steps.then>\n              3. `path:` names the generated test file this scenario's Go\n                 test is written into. REUSE an existing `path:` from a\n                 scenario of the same command or feature family — several\n                 scenarios share one file on purpose, so related\n                 behaviours are read together. Invent a new one only when\n                 no existing file fits, and then make it\n                 `<suite path>/<family>_test.go`, where <suite path> is\n                 the tests/<service>/ tree of the scenario\n                 whose `service:` matches this scenario's.\n              4. Preserve existing file ordering and indentation. Do not\n                 touch any other entry.\n","numLines":69,"startLine":1,"totalLines":69}}}
